	(text "LA pull-ups and pull-downs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b2a7cbba-59c4-4579-9759-41792aac329e")
	)
	(text "Two pull resistors per LA channel, both on the J1 side of the LSF0108 (An_B): a 10k and a 2.2k, both from the same expander: U54 for LA1-LA7 and LA9, U18 for LA8 and LA10-LA14.\nEach port: high = pull-up to VREF_OUT, low = pull-down to GND, input = off. Per channel: 10k, 2.2k or both (about 1.8k),\nup or down. Firmware picks the strength from the pin function (I2C 2.2k, UART RX 10k, 5 V SPI outputs 2.2k).\nKeep both ports of a channel in the same direction (opposite = a divider that draws current).\nVREF_OUT follows LA_VCCIO (1.8 / 3.3 V) or 5 V, so the pulls follow the I/O voltage; in 5 V mode a pull-up lifts a pod-driven high to 5 V.\nPULL_RST (PG7) low = both expanders in reset, all ports inputs, pulls off. R64 holds it low while the STM32 boots;\nfirmware turns VREF_OUT on first, then releases PULL_RST (TI: ramp VCCP before VCCI, else SDA can stick low).\nOld firmware (TCA9554 driver at 0x20) only reaches U18 output/input registers, never its direction registers: pulls stay off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1fd8999f-6349-47f6-a56e-deb6eb5699bb")
	)
